+<a name="id30510"></a><h2>Description</h2>
 <p>An attribute set is an associative container with attribute name as a key and pointer to the attribute as a mapped value. The container allows storing only one element for each distinct key value. In most regards attribute set container provides interface similar to <code class="computeroutput">std::unordered_map</code>. However, there are differences in <code class="computeroutput">operator</code>[] semantics and a number of optimizations with regard to iteration. Besides, attribute names are stored as a read-only <code class="computeroutput"><a class="link" href="classboost_1_1log_1_1attribute__name.html" title="Class attribute_name">attribute_name</a></code>'s instead of <code class="computeroutput">std::string</code>, which saves memory and CPU time. </p>
