-      <span class="phrase"><a name="log.changelog.2_32__boost_1_89"></a></span><a class="link" href="changelog.html#log.changelog.2_32__boost_1_89">2.32,
-      Boost 1.89</a>
-    </h4>
-<div class="itemizedlist"><ul class="itemizedlist" style="list-style-type: disc; ">
-<li class="listitem">
-          Added support for <code class="computeroutput"><span class="identifier">BOOST_LOG_WITHOUT_ASIO</span></code>
-          configuration macro, which can be used to remove the dependency on <a href="https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/doc/html/boost_asio.html" target="_top">Boost.Asio</a>
-          and disable the related functionality.
-        </li>
-<li class="listitem">
-          Use locale-independent formatting of the file counter in <code class="computeroutput"><span class="identifier">text_file_backend</span></code> when composing log
-          file names. This fixes failures in the subsequent parsing of the file names
-          in <code class="computeroutput"><span class="identifier">file_collector</span><span class="special">::</span><span class="identifier">scan_for_files</span></code>. (<a href="https://github.com/boostorg/log/pull/246" target="_top">PR#246</a>)
-        </li>
-<li class="listitem">
-          Added a new <a class="link" href="detailed/expressions.html#log.detailed.expressions.predicates.wrap_filter" title="Injecting user-defined functions in filtering expressions"><code class="computeroutput"><span class="identifier">wrap_filter</span></code></a> utility that simplifies
-          injecting user-defined function objects in filtering expressions. (<a href="https://github.com/boostorg/log/issues/195" target="_top">GH#195</a>)
-        </li>
-</ul></div>
